LiquidLaneConnector
├── initialization
│   ├── rejects zero adapter or funding asset
│   ├── allows an empty token list for registration after deployment
│   └── nonempty token list
│       ├── requires approvals for the predicted connector address
│       ├── rejects zero, funding, duplicate, and unapproved tokens atomically
│       └── saves existing oracles without deploying new ones
├── addTokenToRedeem
│   ├── requires the bound adapter and its own Merkle leaf role
│   ├── rejects zero, funding, duplicate, and unapproved tokens
│   ├── resolves only the connector proxy's registry key
│   └── saves the approved oracle and emits the addition
├── removeTokenToRedeem
│   ├── requires the bound adapter and its own Merkle leaf role
│   ├── rejects unknown tokens, including an empty list
│   └── configured token
│       ├── clears the oracle and removes the list entry without duplicates
│       ├── disables quoting, swapping, and budget reconfiguration
│       └── preserves budget configuration, usage, and inventory
├── registry update
│   ├── only the registry owner can set, replace, or clear exact-pair approvals
│   ├── existing saved oracles remain active after replacement or revocation
│   └── remove followed by add in one MerkleAdapter.manage transaction
│       ├── accepts the replacement without resetting the budget
│       └── rolls back removal if the new approval is missing
├── swap
│   ├── checks inventory, saved oracle price, and per-token budget
│   ├── transfers RWA to the adapter and funding tokens to the recipient
│   ├── rolls back transfers and budget on failure
│   └── rejects reentrant token-list or budget changes
├── signed exact swap
│   ├── requires the bound adapter and the signed caller
│   ├── accepts only the current owner or configured signer, including ERC1271
│   ├── binds every field, connector proxy, and chain in the EIP712 signature
│   ├── rejects expired deadlines, consumed or invalidated nonces, and revoked signers
│   ├── consumes its token-scoped nonce exactly once, shared with discount invalidation
│   ├── enforces the saved oracle quote and shared per-token budget
│   └── rolls back nonce, transfers, and budget on failure or reentrancy
├── signed discount swap
│   ├── requires the bound adapter even when both signatures are valid
│   ├── accepts only the current owner or the single configured signer
│   ├── validates both signatures at execution, supporting revocable ERC1271 signatures
│   ├── binds signatures to the connector proxy and chain, including protocol countersignature
│   ├── rejects either expired deadline, invalidated nonce, or out-of-range discount
│   ├── permits repeated fills until expiry or token-scoped nonce invalidation
│   ├── applies the owner's current minimum discount and the shared token budget
│   ├── transfers the oracle-priced RWA amount and discounted funding amount atomically
│   └── rejects reentrant signer, discount, or nonce configuration
├── signed discount configuration
│   ├── only the owner may replace the signer or change minimum discounts
│   ├── only the owner or current signer may invalidate token-scoped nonces
│   └── signer replacement and ownership transfer revoke old signing authority
└── migration
    ├── preserves tokens, saved oracles, funding asset, budgets, signer, minimums, and nonces
    └── rejects nonempty migration data
